Package: msAUC
Title: Area-Under-the-Curve Estimation of Cumulative Disease Burden
Version: 0.1.1
Authors@R: c(
    person("Jiren", "Sun", email = "jirensun@outlook.com",
           role = c("aut", "cre")),
    person("Tuo", "Wang", role = "aut"),
    person("Yu", "Du", role = "aut"))
Description: Quantifies cumulative disease burden in clinical trials with a
    progressive, ordinal multistate outcome and a terminal event. The estimand
    is the area under the mean cumulative severity-score curve over a
    restriction window, summarised as a ratio and a difference between two
    treatment arms with a per-state decomposition. Users choose which ordinal
    states enter the composite, enabling endpoint-definition sensitivity
    analyses. Inference uses the martingale influence-function representation of
    the restricted mean survival time. Methods follow Claggett and others
    (2018) <doi:10.1002/sim.7907> and Sun and others (2025)
    <doi:10.1002/sim.70187>.
